    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Marine heat waves",
    "problem": "The scientific community has a limited understanding of the physical drivers, future changes, and full ecological and socioeconomic impacts of marine heat waves, which hinders the ability to predict their evolution and mitigate their risks.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a multi-faceted research approach integrating novel data synthesis, high-resolution Earth System Models, and probabilistic event attribution to assess, quantify, and project the future risks of marine heat waves.",
    "task": "The task is to review the current understanding of marine heat waves, their devastating impacts on ecosystems, and to highlight the urgent need for research to predict their future changes and risks in a warming world.",
